the hogwarts express is one of the most  instantly recognizable props in the  entire harry potter series but given the  late 1800s time frame for hogwarts  legacy does it belong in the video game  is the hogwarts express actually a giant  plot hole i think we could actually see  a brand new take on the iconic  locomotive and in today's video i'll  explain why retroreckons who are here  i'm just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell and i've noticed  there's a lot of confusion online about  the hogwarts express specifically when  it was originally created i have a  theory as to why and i think it's  primarily due to three reasons number  one google search results two an error  by jk rowling and three the appearance  of the train in the movies let's start  with the google search at the time of  this recording if you were to go online  and google when was the hogwarts express  built you would see the following as a  highlighted answer notice the section in  bold that says april of 1937. as a  result of this i've noticed a lot of  fans online assuming the hogwarts  express wouldn't be in the game since it  takes place in the late 1800s but we  need to read the full excerpt first  they're citing the hp wiki in this  particular bit is actually referencing a  video where the hogwarts express theme  park actor at the wizarding world of  harry potter said the train was a gwr  model 5900 that was built in 1936. in  reality the gwr 5900 doesn't exist and  the locomotive at the theme park is a  gwr 4900 which was built in 1937. but i  would argue that when folks search about  the hogwarts express on google they're  far more likely to be asking when the  fictional model of the original book  series was designed and not the model at  the wizarding world of harry potter in  orlando florida if you agree you can  actually submit feedback to google on  this answer by clicking the little  feedback icon just here so when did jk  rowling intend for the train to have  been built within the canon of the  series using information compiled from  the original series from pottermore and  even cursed child we're left with the  following the minister of magic in the  year 1827 audelene gamble proposed a  muggle solution to the wizarding world  problem of transporting hundreds of  students to a magic school without  attracting the attention of muggles  prior to this point witches and wizards  had been using a variety of methods to  travel to the school including magical  creatures broomsticks and even portkeys  now unsurprisingly pureblood families  weren't too pleased with gamble's  suggestion to use a muggle technology  however she would ultimately go through  with the plan anyway she commissioned  muggle engineers at a company called  crew works to build the train now crew  works is actually a real world company  but more on that in one second now both  the terrain and its tracks were  completed in 1803 but here's the problem  jk rowling made a bit of a continuity  error here because crew at least in the  real world wasn't built until 1840.  king's cross station also wasn't open  for passengers until october of 1852.  now of course here's where i have to  point out that yes this is all fiction  and there are going to be some little  details like this that are off and don't  quite line up from time to time okay  back to the canon though the ministry of  magic used the biggest concealment charm  britain had ever seen as well as 167  memory charms to move the hogwarts  express the muggle engineers all awoke  the next morning with a feeling they had  misplaced something but they couldn't  remember what something very very large  the ministry would issue a decree that  required all hogwarts students to travel  via the hogwarts express or not attend  at all of course we all know what  happened in harry potter in the chamber  of secrets when he and ron missed the  train  the crane leaves at exactly 11 o'clock  we've missed it  harry  if we can't get through  maybe mom and dad can't get back now  honestly i think rowling could attempt  to clear this up a bit and make it line  up more with the real world history i  would also argue that google should  change this search result to match the  canon answer rather than using an answer  from the theme park actor as for  hogwarts legacy even with the continuity  errors surrounding king's cross and the  crew works company we should definitely  be seeing the hogwarts express by the  late 1800s which is when the game is set  to take place but then we have to decide  what the train should look like and  that's where our third problem comes  into play how it's pictured in the  movies look the train pictured here is  iconic and it's most likely what all of  us are thinking when we imagine the  hogwarts express the train used for the  films is a castle class steam locomotive  number 5972  known as olton hall this particular  model wasn't actually developed until  around the 1930s there's a fairly  detailed reddit post that breaks down  both the locomotive itself as well as  the carriages we see in the movie i'll  link it down in the video description  below the too long didn't read for the  post is essentially if the devs want to  be true to the late 1800s time period  then the hogwarts express and its  carriages should look radically  different than what we see in the films  i'll be honest with you guys for me  personally i'd be totally fine with them  leaving the hogwarts express exactly as  we see it in the movies i know some like  those in the reddit post above are  passionate about maintaining the  historical accuracy and i get it but for  me it's just not something that would  personally break the immersion for me  because that movie design is so iconic i  wouldn't be surprised at all if the devs  at avalanche are just like hey let's  just stick with that design now that  being said if i could choose if i could  decide what's going to happen i would  prefer that they go ahead and change it  preferably to something that's their own  interpretation and also something that  would fit within the late 1800s time  frame if they really wanted to go the  extra mile then we should see some  slight tweaks to the design that would  better match the type of locomotive  likely to have been designed for the  ministry back in 1827. now that reddit  post i mentioned there's also some  comments about what a train from that  time period if it was made that early  what it would have looked like so again  i don't know if they're going to be that  historically accurate i think they  certainly should have the creative  freedom to change things up a bit if  they want after all we are talking about  art here and art is always subject to  interpretation consider that the  hogwarts express in the movies doesn't  match up exactly with the train featured  on the cover of the original british  version of harry potter and the  philosopher's stone also in 2015 artist  jim k had a completely different take  for the hogwarts express which appeared  on the front cover of the new  illustrated edition of sorcerer's stone  now some fans in that very same reddit  post i mentioned earlier seem to think  there's a chance we won't see the  hogwarts express at all given that the  trailer shows someone arriving to the  school by carriage according to the  canon though this would actually be  against the rules put in place by the  ministry once the hogwarts express was  implemented it is the required method of  transportation for students when  traveling to and from the school of  course we also know they don't always  land right there on the hogwarts crowds  it depends on what year they are in  school we all know about the first years  and how they sail across on the black  lake and then there are various other  ways that harry gets to the school  throughout the rest of the books now we  do already know that our character  receives a late acceptance letter to  attend hogwarts which means i guess that  it's possible our student could require  a special mode of transportation to the  school if they're arriving after  everyone else i'm not quite sure that's  what they mean though by late acceptance  letter if the old leaks hold to be true  then that late acceptance letter  actually refers to our character  starting school in year 5 rather than as  a traditional first year we don't really  know why that's the case just yet for my  personal take i think it would really be  a shame if we don't travel to the school  in the hogwarts express at least see it  in a cut scene just considering how  iconic it is for the entire series and  according to the canon in the late 1800s  all students should be required to  travel to hogwarts on the hogwarts  express do you guys want to see the  hogwarts express in the game and if so  are you hoping avalanche will change its  design let me know in the comments below  if you're new here i've got some videos  on the left and right of the screen that  i think you would really love as always  guys thank you all so much for watching  i'll talk to you again soon
 

